                                                                  6228 1451
  General methodology: The global approach considered in this     6228 1451
          work is presented in the following paper: Modern        6228 1451
          nuclear data evaluation with the TALYS code system,     6228 1451
          A.J. Koning and D. Rochman, Nuclear Data Sheets 113     6228 1451
          (2012) 2841.                                            6228 1451
                                                                  6228 1451
  MF2:  Resolved resonance range  (RRR)                           6228 1451
       The RRR was generated with TARES-1.31, compiled on         6228 1451
       12-10-2015 11:58:11 PM at Villingen  , Switzerland. The RRR6228 1451
       expands from 0 to 7.465446E+2 eV. A total of               6228 1451
       2 l-values are used and 146 resonances. The resonance      6228 1451
       formalism is multi-level Breit Wigner (MLBW).              6228 1451
       The ladder approach from the CALENDF code is used to       6228 1451
       generate statistical resonances in the unresolved          6228 1451
       resonance range. Therefore, the URR is translated into     6228 1451
       resolved resonance range. Explanations about the method    6228 1451
       can be found in the CALENDF manual: CEA-Report CEA-R-6277  6228 1451
       "CALENDF-2010: User manual" by J.C. Sublet, P. Ribon and   6228 1451
       M. Coste-Delcaux.                                          6228 1451
       The method of creating statistical resonances in the       6228 1451
       URR region is described in: "From average parameters to    6228 1451
       statistical resolved resonances", D. Rochman et al.,       6228 1451
       Annals of Nucl. Ene. 51 (2013) 60.                         6228 1451
       The s-wave average level spacing is 3.632 eV and           6228 1451
       the s-wave neutron strength is 0.0005237 1e-4.             6228 1451
                                                                  6228 1451
       After the ladder method, the retroactive method is applied 6228 1451
       to update the MF32 and MF2 with the SAMMY code.            6228 1451
                                                                  6228 1451
  MF32: Covariance file for resonance parameters                  6228 1451
        The compact format is used to represent the covariance    6228 1451
        information on the resonance parameters. Uncertainties    6228 1451
        come from compilations, EXFOR or existing libraries and   6228 1451
        correlations between parameters are obtained following    6228 1451
        the method presented in NIM/A 589 (2008) 85.              6228 1451
        SAMMY is used in the retroactive mode to update MF32.     6228 1451
                                                                  6228 1451
